e to start  in people's homes pile in the support  there and look after older people  differently and that means a single  budget a single service for Health and  Social Care and voting proposal I'm  plant that is mr. Burnham proposal let  us know what you think about what what  the shadow Secretary has to say on all  of that and that's one aspect of why  we've got pressure on A&amp;E but what else  is contributing to these huge amounts of  people and I put it to you Andy Burnham  as a politician you're just like all the  rest of them you won't actually take  responsibility you won't grab this and  say to the general public look you guys  you're going to have to take some  responsibility as well you charge people  for prescriptions why don't you charge  them five quid or so to attend a and E  and Sweden they get charged 30 quid for  going into A&amp;E well I'd honestly don't  think that that will work even if you  charge people to access services they  don't go for care when they should go a  good thing but not well though what  happens is they get they get more ill  and they end up as a  more expensive patient later down the  line it sounds simple doesn't it sounds  attractive to some people not to move  actually but to some people but in the  end you spend more money because people  don't get care and then they are very  become seriously ill and that cost far  far more than the charge to see you know  what you're a good man to talk to  because you do talk simple and we want  to talk simple to you today because  people look at this and say hi the heck  is there such a mess Isabelle wants to  say something very simple to you we came  up with here was that why don't we have  a GP system at all a Andy's so that  there's a simple triage procedure and  you don't waste the time so those  critical A&amp;E consultants and initiatives  and all of those people who need to deal  with those acute cases you can just go  and see a GP 24 hours a day it's so  simple well exactly t